{
  "title": "66: al-Tahreem التحريم",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ لِمَ تُحَرِّمُ مَاۤ اَحَلَّ اللّٰهُ لَكَ‌ۚ تَبْتَغِىْ مَرْضَاتَ اَزْوَاجِكَ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ غَفُوْرٌ رَّحِيْمٌ‏(1)\nYAA AYYOHAL NABIYYO LEMA TUHARREMU MAA AAHALLA LAAHO LAKA TABTAGHEAA MARZAATA AAZWAAJEKA WAL LAAHO GHAFOORUR RAHEEM.\nO’ (Our) Prophet! Why dost thou forbid (unto thyself) what God hath made lawful unto thee? Thou seekest to please thy wives; and God is Oft-Forgiving, the Most Merciful.\nقَدْ فَرَضَ اللّٰهُ لَكُمْ تَحِلَّةَ اَيْمَانِكُمْ‌ؕ وَاللّٰهُ مَوْلٰٮكُمْ‌ۚ وَهُوَ الْعَلِيْمُ الْحَكِيْمُ‏(2)\nQAD FARAZA LAAHO LAKUM TAHELLATA AAYMAANEKUM WAL LAAHO MAWLAAKUM WA HOWA A’LEEM HAKEEM.\nIndeed hath God made lawful for you the dissolution of your oaths (in such cases), and God (alone) is your Lord, and He is the All-Knowing, the All-Wise.\nوَاِذْ اَسَرَّ النَّبِىُّ اِلٰى بَعْضِ اَزْوَاجِهٖ حَدِيْثًا‌ۚ فَلَمَّا نَبَّاَتْ بِهٖ وَاَظْهَرَهُ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ عَرَّفَ بَعْضَهٗ وَاَعْرَضَ عَنْۢ بَعْضٍ‌ۚ فَلَمَّا نَبَّاَهَا بِهٖ قَالَتْ مَنْ اَنْۢبَاَكَ هٰذَا‌ؕ قَالَ نَبَّاَنِىَ الْعَلِيْمُ الْخَبِیْرُ‏(3)\nWA IZ AASARRA NABIYYO ELAA BAA’ZE AAZWAAJEH HADEESAN FALAMMAA NABBAAT BEHI WAAZHARAHU LAAHO A’LAYHE A’ARRAFA BAA’ZAH WA A-A’RAZA A’N ELAA FALAMMAA NABBAAHAA BEHI QAALAT MAN AANBAAKA HAAZAA QAALA NABBAANEAAA A’LEEM AL-KHABERU.\nWhen the Prophet confided unto one of his wives a matter, but when she divulged it (unto others) and God apprised him thereof, he made known a part of it and avoided a part; so when he informed her of it, said she: “Who informed thee of this?” He said: “Informed, me, the All-Knowing, the All-Aware.\nاِنْ تَتُوْبَاۤ اِلَى اللّٰهِ فَقَدْ صَغَتْ قُلُوْبُكُمَا‌ۚ وَاِنْ تَظٰهَرَا عَلَيْهِ فَاِنَّ اللّٰهَ هُوَ مَوْلٰٮهُ وَجِبْرِيْلُ وَصَالِحُ الْمُؤْمِنِيْنَ‌ۚ وَالْمَلٰٓئِكَةُ بَعْدَ ذٰلِكَ ظَهِيْرٌ‏(4)\nIN TATOOBAA ELAL LAAHE FAQAD SAGHAT QULOOBUKUMAA WA TAZAAHARAA A’LAYHE FA-INNAL LAAHA HOWA MAWLAAHU WAJEBREELU WASAALEHU MOAMENEEN WAL MALAAA-EKATO BA’DA ZAALEKA ZAHEERUN.\nIf ye two turn (in repentance) unto Him, then indeed your hearts are inclined (to this) but if ye two back up each other against him, then verily God it is Who is his Protector, and Gabriel, and the (most) Virtuous one among the believers, and the angels thereafter will back (him)- up.\nعَسٰى رَبُّهٗۤ اِنْ طَلَّقَكُنَّ اَنْ يُّبْدِلَهٗۤ اَزْوَاجًا خَيْرًا مِّنْكُنَّ مُسْلِمٰتٍ مُّؤْمِنٰتٍ قٰنِتٰتٍ تٰٓئِبٰتٍ عٰبِدٰتٍ سٰٓئِحٰتٍ ثَيِّبٰتٍ وَّاَبْكَارًا‏(5)\nA’SAA RABBOHU IN TALLAQAKUNNA AN YYUBDELAH AZWAAJANW KHAYRAN MMENKUNNA MUSLEMAATIN MMUMENAATIN QAANETAATIN TAAAEBAATIN A’AABEDAATIN SAAAEHAATIN SAYBAATIN WWAABKAARAN.\nHapply his Lord if he divorceth you, will give him in your place wives better than you, submissive, faithful, obedient, repentant, prayerful, observers of fast, widows and virgins.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا قُوْۤا اَنْفُسَكُمْ وَاَهْلِيْكُمْ نَارًا وَّقُوْدُهَا النَّاسُ وَالْحِجَارَةُ عَلَيْهَا مَلٰٓئِكَةٌ غِلَاظٌ شِدَادٌ لَّا يَعْصُوْنَ اللّٰهَ مَاۤ اَمَرَهُمْ وَيَفْعَلُوْنَ مَا يُؤْمَرُوْنَ‏(6)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO QOOA ANFOSAKUM WAAHLEEKUM NAARAN WWAQOODUHAA NAASO WAL HEJAARAH A’LAYHAA MALAAAEKATUN GHELAAZUN SHEDAADUN LAA YAA’SOONA LAAHA MAA AAMARAHUM WA YAF-A’LOON MAA YUMAROONA.\nO’ ye who believe! Save yourselves and your families from the fire whose fuel shall be men and stones; over which shall be angels stern and strong, they disobey not God in what He commandeth them, and act (only) as they are bidden.\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا لَا تَعْتَذِرُوا الْيَوْمَ‌ؕ اِنَّمَا تُجْزَوْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(7)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA KAFAROO LAA TAA’TAZEROOA AL-YAWMA INNAMAA TUJZAWNA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n(Will say the Angels) “O’ ye who disbelieve! Make ye not excuses this day; ye shall be recompensed as ye used to do!\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا الَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا تُوْبُوْۤا اِلَى اللّٰهِ تَوْبَةً نَّصُوْحًا ؕ عَسٰى رَبُّكُمْ اَنْ يُّكَفِّرَ عَنْكُمْ سَيِّاٰتِكُمْ وَيُدْخِلَكُمْ جَنّٰتٍ تَجْرِىْ مِنْ تَحْتِهَا الْاَنْهٰرُ ۙ يَوْمَ لَا يُخْزِى اللّٰهُ النَّبِىَّ وَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا مَعَهٗ‌ ۚ نُوْرُهُمْ يَسْعٰى بَيْنَ اَيْدِيْهِمْ وَبِاَيْمَانِهِمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ رَبَّنَاۤ اَ تْمِمْ لَنَا نُوْرَنَا وَاغْفِرْ لَنَا‌ ۚ اِنَّكَ عَلٰى كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيْرٌ‏(8)\nYAA AYYOHAL LAZEENA AAMANOO TOOBOOA ELAL LAAHE TAWBATAN NNASOOHAN A’SAA RABBOKUM AN YYUKAFFERA A’NKUM SAYAAATEKUM WAYUDKHELAKUM JANNAATIN TAJREE MIN TAHTEHAL ANHAARO YAWMA LAA YUKHZEAA LAAHO NABIYYA WAL LAZEENA AAMANOO MA-A’HU NOORUHUM YAS-A’A BAYNA AYDEEHIM WABEAAYMAANEHEM YAQOOLOONA RABBANAA A’ZAABAN TMEM LANAA NOORANAA FIRLANAA LANAA INNAKA A’LAA KULLE SHAY-IN QADEER.\nO’ ye who believe! Turn ye (in repentance) unto God with a turning of sincere penitence; happily your Lord will wipe out from you your sins and admit you into gardens ‘neath which flow rivers, on the day, God will abase not the Prophet and those who believe with him; their light will run before them and on their right hand; they shall (prayerfully) say: “O’ Our Lord! Perfect for us our light, and grant us forgiveness! Verily Thou (O’ Our Lord!) over all things, art the All-Powerful (One).\nيٰۤاَيُّهَا النَّبِىُّ جَاهِدِ الْكُفَّارَ وَالْمُنٰفِقِيْنَ وَاغْلُظْ عَلَيْهِمْ‌ؕ وَمَاْوٰٮهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ‌ؕ وَبِئْسَ الْمَصِيْرُ‏(9)\nYAA AYYOHAL NABIYYO JAAHEDE KUFFAARA KAAFEREENA WAAGHLUZ WA WAMAAWAAHUM JAHANNAM WA WA BEASAL MASEER.\nO’ (Our) Prophet! strive thou against the disbelievers and the hypocrites, and be thou hard against them; And their abode is hell; And evil is (their) destination.\nضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا لِّلَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوا امْرَاَتَ نُوْحٍ وَّ امْرَاَتَ لُوْطٍ‌ ؕ كَانَتَا تَحْتَ عَبْدَيْنِ مِنْ عِبَادِنَا صَالِحَيْنِ فَخَانَتٰهُمَا فَلَمْ يُغْنِيَا عَنْهُمَا مِنَ اللّٰهِ شَيْئًا وَّقِيْلَ ادْخُلَا النَّارَ مَعَ الدّٰخِلِيْنَ‏(10)\nZARABA LAAHO MASALAA LIL-LAZEENA KAFARUL AMRAATA NOOHIN WA AMRAATA LOOTIM KAANATAA TAHTA A’ABDAYNE MIN E’EBAADENAA SAALEHAYNE FAKHAANATAAHUMAA FALAM YUGHNEEA A’ANHUMAA MENAL LAAHE SHAY-ANW WWAQEELA ADKHULAA NAARAL LAAHA AD-DAAKHELEENA.\nSetteth forth God the similitude unto those who disbelieve the wife of Noah, and the wife of Lot; they both were under two of Our righteous servants, but they two were unfaithful (unto their husbands) and they (their husbands) availed them naught against God, and it was said (unto them)’, “Enter ye both the fire (along) with those who enter (it)?\nوَضَرَبَ اللّٰهُ مَثَلًا لِّلَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا امْرَاَتَ فِرْعَوْنَ‌ۘ اِذْ قَالَتْ رَبِّ ابْنِ لِىْ عِنْدَكَ بَيْتًا فِى الْجَنَّةِ وَنَجِّنِىْ مِنْ فِرْعَوْنَ وَعَمَلِهٖ وَنَجِّنِىْ مِنَ الْقَوْمِ الظّٰلِمِيْنَۙ‏(11)\nWA ZARABA LAAHO MASALAA LIL-LAZEENA AAMANOO AMRAATA FIR-A’WNA IZ QAALAT RABBE MARYAM LEE E’ENDAKA BAYTAN FIL JANNAH WA NAJJENEE MIN FIR-A’WNA WAA’AMALEH WA NAJJENEE MENAL QAWMIL ZAALEMEEN.\nSetteth forth God the similitude unto those who believe the wife of Pharaoh, when said she: “O’ My Lord! Build thou for me a house in the Garden and deliver me from Pharaoh and his doing, and deliver me from the unjust people!\nوَمَرْيَمَ ابْنَتَ عِمْرٰنَ الَّتِىْۤ اَحْصَنَتْ فَرْجَهَا فَنَفَخْنَا فِيْهِ مِنْ رُّوْحِنَا وَصَدَّقَتْ بِكَلِمٰتِ رَبِّهَا وَكُتُبِهٖ وَكَانَتْ مِنَ الْقٰنِتِيْنَ‏(12)\nWA MARYAMAL ABNATA E’EMRAANA LATEE AAHSANAT FARJAHAA FANAFAKHNAA FEEHE MIN RROOHENAA WASADDAQAT BEKALEMAATE RABBEHAA WA KOTOBEHI WA KAANAT MENAL AL-QAANETEENA.\nAnd Mary the daughter of Imran, who guarded her chastity; and breathed We into it (her body) of Our Spirit, and she testified the truth of the words of her Lord, and His Scriptures, and she was of the obedient ones.",
  "merits": "Surah al-Tahreem (The Prohibition)\nThis ‘Madani’ Surah has 12 verses. It is narrated from the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) that the one who recites this Surah will be from those who always seek sincere repentance from Allah (s.w.t.). The recitation of this Surah and drinking of its water acts as a cure from many ailments and diseases.\nIf this Surah is recited by a person who is not getting sleep then he will be able to sleep and if recited by a person who is frightened, he will become calm. Frequent recitation also helps a person who is in debt to clear his debts."
